# UI quality

- Follow `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`; the visible connection rail is the defining visual device.
- Use Familjen Grotesk for interface copy and DM Mono for room/network identifiers.
- Use Lucide icons, never emoji or text glyphs as interface icons.
- Use square structural borders; avoid turning every region into a floating rounded card.
- Keep controls at least 44px tall where space permits and provide visible `:focus-visible` states.
- Pair every connection color with a text label and screen-reader status update.
- At narrow widths, hide diagnostics before reducing the conversation's usable width.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; interaction motion must explain a state change.
- Use plain, accurate networking language: “Create a room”, “Copy invite”, and “Try again”.
